## Repo map

```
src/app/        Next.js App Router routes — THIN (re-export a feature screen, no logic)
src/ui/         Design-system primitives + theme/ (colors · spacing · typography · motion · icons)
src/features/   One folder per feature: screens/ components/ hooks/ api/ types
src/api/        Cross-feature data layer: clients/ (requests) + queries/ (React Query)
src/utilities/  Shared pure helpers (dates, formatters, …)
src/providers/  App-level context providers ('use client'; mounted in src/app/layout.tsx)
src/constants/  env.ts (hand-validated), enums
src/types/      Cross-cutting types
docs/           design-language.md — the house UI rules; read before UI work
```

Each `src/*` folder has its own `README.md` listing what lives there — read it
before adding files, and add a line when you add something notable.

## Tooling

- Use `bun` for everything (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bunx <bin>`).
- `bun run check` runs the full gate: type-check + lint + fmt +
  `check:structure` + test (the CORE gate order).
- Structure rules are **machine-enforced**, not doc-only: oxlint carries
  `no-restricted-imports` (no barrel imports, no deep relatives, feature
  isolation), `unicorn/filename-case` (kebab-case), and `max-lines` (300);
  `scripts/check-structure.sh` checks the folder tree (allowed `src/` dirs,
  per-folder READMEs, no barrel files).
- `bun run dev` starts the dev server; `bun run build` produces a production build.
- `bun run lint:fix` and `bun run fmt` auto-fix.
- Pre-commit (Lefthook) runs oxlint + oxfmt on staged files.
- Tests run non-interactively via `vitest run`; never leave watch mode in CI.

## Blocked patterns (pre-commit + CI reject these)

- `as any`, `: any`, `as unknown as T` → use `unknown` + type guards.
- `console.log`, `debugger` → use `console.warn` / `console.error`.
- **Barrel files** (an `index.ts` that only re-exports) → import the concrete
  file. The **one carve-out**: `src/app/**` route files, which thinly re-export a
  feature screen as their default export (see Conventions).
- **Default exports outside `src/app/`** → named exports everywhere else.
  `src/app/**` route files are the sanctioned exception (Next.js requires them).
- **Deep relative imports** (`../../…`) → use the `@/` alias.
- **Cross-feature imports** — importing `@/features/*` from anywhere but a
  `src/app/**` route file → features are isolated; only routes pull in a screen.
- **Mock-data tests** — a test that only proves a mock returns what the mock was
  told to return → tests must exercise real inputs and real integration paths.
- Tests outside a sibling `__tests__/`.
- Files over 300 lines (tests exempt) → split.

## Conventions

- **Path alias**: `@/*` → `src/*` (e.g. `@/ui/button`, `@/features/home/...`).
  Never deep relative imports (`../../../ui`).
- **Filenames**: kebab-case, named after the export (`shift-card.tsx` →
  `ShiftCard`; `use-shifts.ts` → `useShifts`). One primary export per file.
- **Default exports** only in `src/app/**` (Next.js requires them for `page` /
  `layout` / `route` / `error` / `loading`); named exports everywhere else.
- **Routes are thin**: a file under `src/app/` imports a feature screen and
  re-exports it — no data fetching, state, or logic in the route file.
- **Server vs. Client Components**: components are **Server Components by
  default**. Add `'use client'` only when the file needs interactivity, React
  state/effects, or browser APIs. Keep the boundary as low in the tree as
  possible; data fetching prefers Server Components / server actions.
- **Styling**: theme tokens from `src/ui/theme/*` (CSS Modules or plain CSS
  referencing the tokens) — no hardcoded hex, no magic numbers.
- **Data**: server state → React Query (`src/api`) on the client, or fetch in
  Server Components; client state → local state / React Context (no store
  library — for genuinely-global client state use `createContext` +
  `useReducer` in `src/providers/`). Never duplicate server data into client
  state.
- **Validation**: env + external/parsed data are validated by hand (type guards
  on `unknown`) — no schema library app-wide. `zod` is allowed **only** inside a
  form (`react-hook-form` + `zodResolver`), scoped to that form.
- **Testing**: co-locate tests in a sibling `__tests__/`, and test with **real
  data** — exercise real inputs and real integration paths. No mock-only tests
  that just replay what a mock was told to return; they hide integration breakage.
- **Doc line required**: every module and public symbol carries a concise
  `/** … */` doc line — brief, but not optional.
- **Docs in sync**: a change to a user-facing surface (behavior, public API,
  routes, config) updates the prose describing it (README, the relevant
  `src/*/README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`) in the **same** change.
- **Commits**: `type(scope): description` (conventional). Push to feature
  branches; never directly to main.

